      "body": "## Purpose\n\nIn a uv-created venv (which has no `pip`), `collect_env` falls back to\n`uv pip list --format=freeze`. That call does not say which environment to\ninspect, so uv discovers one from the working directory. Two things go wrong:\n\n1. **Wrong packages are reported.** When the venv is not activated\n   (e.g. `/path/to/.venv/bin/python -m vllm.collect_env`, or a systemd unit),\n   uv lists a different environment. On my machine the venv had\n   `torch==2.14.1+cpu` / `numpy==2.5.3`, but `collect_env` printed the system\n   environment's `numpy==2.2.6` and `nvidia-*` packages. This is silent and\n   ends up pasted into bug reports.\n2. **It crashes when the command fails.** If `uv` is not on `PATH`, or uv finds\n   no environment, `run_and_read_all` returns `None` and the script dies with\n   `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'splitlines'`\n   (this is the crash mentioned in the environment section of #44538).\n\nThis PR passes `--python sys.executable` so the listed packages belong to the\ninterpreter running the script, and returns `None` when the command fails so\nthe report shows `[pip3] Could not collect` (the existing convention) instead\nof crashing.\n\nFollow-up to #13888 / #15792, which added the uv fallback.\n\n**Not a duplicate:** checked open PRs with `gh pr list --search \"collect_env\"`\nand `--search \"13888 in:body\"`. #48354 touches `get_pkg_version` (non-Linux\nassert) and #39817 touches ROCm reporting; neither changes `get_pip_packages`.\nThe new tests live in `tests/test_collect_env_pip.py` to avoid colliding with\nthe `tests/test_collect_env.py` that #48354 adds.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n```bash\npytest tests/test_collect_env_pip.py -v\nruff check vllm/collect_env.py tests/test_collect_env_pip.py\nruff format --check vllm/collect_env.py tests/test_collect_env_pip.py\n```\n\nManual check in a uv venv without pip:\n\n```bash\n# uv not on PATH\nenv PATH=/usr/bin:/bin .venv/bin/python -m vllm.collect_env\n# venv not activated, run from another directory\ncd /tmp && /path/to/.venv/bin/python -m vllm.collect_env\n```\n\n## Test Result\n\n```\n2 passed\nruff: All checks passed! / 2 files left unchanged\n```\n\nBoth tests fail on `main` with the `AttributeError` above.\n\nManual check:\n\n| Scenario | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `uv` not on `PATH` | `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'splitlines'` | `[pip3] Could not collect` |\n| venv not activated | system packages (`numpy==2.2.6`, `nvidia-*`) | venv packages (`numpy==2.5.3`, `torch==2.14.1+cpu`) |\n\n---\n\nAI assistance disclosure: this PR was prepared with AI (Claude) assistance. I\nhave reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above myself.\n",
